    + "// Read the other way that argument fails. A borrowed array has no producer but\n"
    + "// it does have a traversal — section 8.1's provided `Iterable` row, which\n"
    + "// section 8.2 emits as native `for...of` — and a `Vector(a)` has the producer\n"
    + "// the result needs, `append`, in scope because this module is seated after\n"
    + "// `Vector.hex`. So the fold below is expressible at the same complexity and in\n"
    + "// the same emitted shape a key would have produced, and\n"
    + "// `spec/stdlib-roadmap.md` section 5.1 keeps such behaviour in Hexagon: none of\n"
    + "// its four grounds for a private intrinsic — a host capability, an opaque or\n"
    + "// performance-critical representation, a compiler transformation, measured\n"
    + "// performance evidence — reaches this operation.\n"
    + "//\n"
    + "// The loop is the whole contract. It is eager because it runs to completion\n"
    + "// before the value is returned; it is a snapshot because every element is read\n"
    + "// out of the borrow and into a persistent vector that shares no storage with\n"
    + "// it; it is shallow because the values are moved, never rebuilt; it is total\n"
    + "// because an empty array takes zero steps. Section 6.4's holes need nothing\n"
